{"author":{"id":"a51b5961cc6de343a64125d8eb6a0f965aa434020b9c46ed932a1bbf143eb532"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791582845,"nonce":"QQF5lqstAWBGIinl5kiuTEI6zAg=","message":"Second cause found and fixed in 2724403: a window whose surface refuses frames.\n\nWith the diagnostics from the first fix, the host test then failed 9 of 15 runs in one burst on 2026-10-09 (0 of 25 in the runs before and after). Every failure looked the same: frames 0, a frame pending, visible, not minimized, presentable by the host's account, no Occluded event ever reported, and about 290 failed surface acquisitions in 5 s (one per 16 ms retry). So the system had not put the window on screen (another desktop or a full-screen app in front is the likely case; it never sent an occlusion change because the window started out unseen), while the window reported itself visible and the surface refused every frame.\n\nFix: after three failed acquisitions in a row the host reports the window not presentable, and backs its retries off from 16 ms to at most 500 ms until a frame succeeds or an event (Occluded, Resized, a redraw request) asks for one. Frame waits in the tests already pause while the window is not presentable, and now report the surface state (surfaceMisses, missStreak, occlusionReported, holdingFrame, timerPending, msSinceTick) when they fail. 15 runs of the host test and a full native run passed after it. A window the system never shows still makes a test fail, after the 60 s cap, with that state in the message.","files":null}]}